<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">John Hawkwood</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1323–1394</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Giovanni Acuto</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">John Hawkwood (c. 1323–1394) was an English <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mercenary">mercenary</a> captain who spent most of his career in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, leading the White Company and other bands for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pisa">Pisa</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/papacy">papacy</a> and others. From 1377 he served <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florence">Florence</a> as its captain-general, defending the city against Giangaleazzo Visconti. After his death the republic honoured him with a painted equestrian monument by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paolo-uccello">Paolo Uccello</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florence-cathedral">Florence Cathedral</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/john-hawkwood.jpg" alt="John Hawkwood" width="320" height="425" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:John_hawkwood.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
